WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.149 align:start position:0%
 
not so special for  the san francisco 49ers there have  always been durability concerns when it  comes to the bosa brothers and nick bosa  suffered an ankle sprain in practice on  wednesday may not play at all in the  preseason he got an mri on wednesday  evening the 49ers gonna be cautious as  he works his way back from the injury  trying to get him ready for week one now  remember when his brother joey came out  three years ago from ohio state he he  was a holdout at this stage of the  calendar so uh it took him time to even  get in and then he did have some injury  issues and that's always been one of the  concerns and and like not to jinx  anybody we were talking about hey there  hasn't been a really big injury to a key  player that's knocked him out for the  season yet and for a while yesterday  there was some anxiety about  uh  nick bosa possibly having a serious  injury but uh for now  not serious but he's had two injuries he  hasn't played in the game  and uh  you're gonna hold your breath if you're  a 49ers fan especially because they  could have had quinn and williams and  and you know usually you see those  apples to apples comparisons with  quarterbacks or running backs or  receivers but when the 49ers had quinn  and williams on the board and there was  some buzz that maybe they were going to  take him that maybe he was the safer  pick  and remember all that that the off-field  stuff with both so not that he got in  any trouble but there was some concern  about political issues and would that  fly in san francisco and and that all  got pushed aside they went with the guy  who has the higher upside in their  estimation but it could be that quinn  and williams ends up being the guy that  uh that has the stronger  um  chance at least to make an impact right  away and d ford also has tendonitis in  his knee he's not available right now  and he here we are  the 49ers every time it feels like  they're trying to get the ducks in a row  to go out and have  a contending relevant team under kyle  shanahan this injury issue pops up and  it's popped up with various different  guys uh and and you know at a certain  point  it's no longer bad luck and i've said  this many times over the years i  remember it happened with the seahawks  10 years ago there's been issues at  times with teams like the chargers  when you have more injuries than you  should at a certain point it really  isn't just dumb luck  at a certain point you have to go back  and take a look at  your training strength programs you have  to look at your rehab you have to look  at everything is there something that  you're not doing or you or that you are  doing incorrectly that is setting the  stage for or contributing to these  injuries if you watch games on sunday  it's amazing how many guys you see get  all pretzeled up and and they're fine  they get up and they they walk away from  it a lot of that is a testament to the  things that their teams do to get them  ready to go out there and play and when  guys are getting injured all the time  that's when you really need to take a  closer look at what's going on and as  stats points out they did fire their  head trainer last year so they're at  least i think on notice that something's  not right there and uh if you're a 49ers  fan again if you're a fan of any team  you're holding your breath in the  preseason for the possibility of an  injury to a key player you don't want to  have that happen and for some teams  you're you're really holding your breath  because you've you've come to accept  that  it's just a matter of time before that  one injury happens it's going to derail  all of that optimism that you have built  into the run-up to the season and really  we're getting close to that point where  bubbles are going to start to pop  all off season long  plenty of  hope and plenty of excitement and plenty  of connecting at the dots to come to the  conclusion that hey this is the year  this could be the year and then reality  starts to set in in the preseason it  sets in with injury or maybe guys just  don't look very good and then when you  start piling up losses in september and  october  that's when that's when you start  thinking about next year when you get to  be zero and zero and be full of hope and  optimism all over again and that's one  of the things even though we have seen  the patriots essentially own the nfl for  the past generation with six super bowl  championships there's still a sense that  in any given year  any given team can't find their way to  the playoffs and we've seen it enough  times where a team  gets a spot low on the playoff tree and  runs the table that  it's stupid as it sounds and there isn't  a team this year that i would say has no  chance of making the playoffs in past  years i remember a year where i said the  raiders have no chance of making the  playoffs and then i worried oh my god  they're going to turn it around and make  me look like even more of an idiot than  i already am but they didn't that year  there was a year i said the browns have  no chance this year  there isn't a team that i can point at  and say that team has no chance some  would say miami i think under brian  flores they have a chance to at least  get lucky to at least put some wins  together build some confidence you know  every team is going to get better or  worse than they are right out of the  gates and we have seen teams get  dramatically better by the end of the  regular season and i don't think there's  a team out of the 32 uh that are in the  nfl that i would look at and say it's  impossible for them to get good enough  to steal one of the six playoff spots in  either conference by the time the dust  settles but that process begins tonight  of getting to  the preseason getting to see the rookies  getting to worry about injuries getting  to see football again the uniforms are  back out it's going to look like exactly  what it will look like in september it  just doesn't mean anything in the  standings but for now it's what we have  and we can't wait to see  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

